<!-- [XPLAT] migrated from net48/WinForms — see MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md -->
<!--
    [XPLAT] AgOpenGPS (GPS program) — "Move / Nudge Reference Track" tool palette (Avalonia view).

    1:1 PARITY reimplementation of the WinForms `Forms/Guidance/FormRefNudge` (source:
    FormRefNudge.cs + FormRefNudge.designer.cs — note the WinForms designer file name was the
    lowercase `FormRefNudge.designer.cs`; that case hazard is resolved here). Per AAP section 0.3.3
    this is visual + behavioural FIDELITY to the currently rendered Windows Forms UI, never a
    redesign: no new colours, no relayout, no UX changes. The palette nudges the active reference
    track sideways by a snap distance (half-tool or fixed) and offers a Cancel that rolls the track
    list back to a snapshot.

    SHELL — mirrors FormRefNudge.designer.cs (lines 219-238) exactly:
      Text "Ref Adjust !!!!!" (design)  : Title. The runtime caption is set by the partner
                                          code-behind to gStr.gsNudgeRefTrack ("Move Reference
                                          Track"); the literal here is a readable design-time
                                          placeholder showing that runtime value.
      ClientSize 223 x 396              : a 223 x 396 Canvas + SizeToContent="WidthAndHeight", so the
                                          CLIENT area is exactly 223 x 396 regardless of the OS
                                          decorations drawn around it. (A literal Window Width/Height
                                          on a DECORATED window would shrink the client by the
                                          caption-bar height and clip the bottom OK / Cancel buttons,
                                          whose lowest edge is at y=391.) This is the same approach
                                          the sibling FixedDialog views FormHelpView and
                                          FormShiftPosView use. [XPLAT] minor chrome-size variance
                                          across OSes is acceptable.
      BackColor Color.LightCoral        : Background="LightCoral". FIXED palette (not day/night
                                          themed): FormRefNudge was never part of SwapDayNightMode,
                                          so the App.axaml Aog* brushes are deliberately NOT used
                                          here (parity).
      FormBorderStyle.FixedDialog       : SystemDecorations="Full" + CanResize="False" (a decorated,
                                          non-resizable dialog that keeps its caption bar).
      ControlBox = false /              : [XPLAT] WinForms ControlBox=false (keep the caption but
      MaximizeBox = false /               hide the system min / max / close buttons) has no portable
      MinimizeBox = false                 Avalonia equivalent. SystemDecorations="Full" + the OS
                                          title bar is the closest approximation, so the OS chrome
                                          may still show those buttons; this is a benign chrome-only
                                          variance — the in-form btnExit (commit) and btnCancelMain
                                          (rollback) remain the primary affordances exactly as before.
      ShowInTaskbar = false             : ShowInTaskbar="False".
      StartPosition = CenterParent      : WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner". The source's
                                          position-restore lines are commented out, so NO saved
                                          location / size is restored (parity).
      (no TopMost in the source)        : Topmost is intentionally NOT set (parity).
      Font (form default)               : FontFamily="Tahoma"; children carry their point sizes
                                          converted to Avalonia DIP as (pt * 96 / 72): 18pt -> 24,
                                          15.75pt -> 21.

    NAMESPACE — x:Class uses the FLAT namespace "AgOpenGPS.Views" (NOT "AgOpenGPS.Views.Guidance")
    even though this file lives in the Views/Guidance/ folder, exactly as the file specification
    mandates. C# / Avalonia namespaces are independent of folder location, so this is valid and the
    partner code-behind (FormRefNudgeView.axaml.cs) declares the matching
    `namespace AgOpenGPS.Views { public partial class FormRefNudgeView : Window }`.

    ASSETS — button glyphs are served from the GPS assembly ("AgOpenGPS") via avares:// URIs from
    the btnImages/ folder (avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/{SnapLeftHalf, SnapRightHalf, SnapLeft,
    SnapRight, Cancel64, OK64}.png — each a native 64 x 64 asset). [XPLAT] the file spec named a
    "Resources/" folder, but the actual PNGs live in GPS/btnImages/ (the Resources/ folder holds
    only .wav audio), and every sibling GPS Avalonia view references these same glyphs via
    btnImages/ — so btnImages/ is used here to keep the glyphs loading; a Resources/ path would
    fail to resolve and break the 1:1 visual parity.

    WIRING CONTRACT — the partner code-behind (FormRefNudgeView.axaml.cs) owns ALL behaviour. This
    view is CODE-BEHIND DRIVEN: intentionally NO x:DataType, NO DataContext, NO {Binding}. The
    x:Name'd controls below are the entire integration surface and keep their ORIGINAL WinForms
    names so the migrated handlers address them exactly as FormRefNudge.cs did. No Click handlers
    are wired in this markup — the code-behind attaches them by name (btnAdjLeft_Click,
    btnAdjRight_Click, btnHalfToolLeft_Click, btnHalfToolRight_Click, nudSnapDistance_Click,
    btnExit_Click, btnCancelMain_Click) — so the .axaml and .axaml.cs can be authored independently
    in parallel:
      - btnHalfToolLeft / btnHalfToolRight : nudge the track left / right by half of
                                             (tool.width - tool.overlap).
      - btnAdjLeft / btnAdjRight           : nudge the track left / right by the snap distance.
      - nudSnapDistance                    : read-only snap-distance display; a click opens the
                                             on-screen numeric keypad (FormNumeric) in code-behind.
      - lblOffset                          : running total offset readout (code-behind sets the text
                                             to e.g. "12 cm").
      - btnExit                            : commit (saves the track list) and close.
      - btnCancelMain                      : roll the track list back to the snapshot and close.

    No WinForms, no OpenTK, no GMap, no ColorPicker types are referenced — Avalonia 11.3.0 only.
-->
<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        x:Class="AgOpenGPS.Views.FormRefNudgeView"
        Title="Move Reference Track"
        SystemDecorations="Full"
        SizeToContent="WidthAndHeight"
        CanResize="False"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner"
        Background="LightCoral"
        FontFamily="Tahoma">

    <!--
        Shared styles.

        Button.imageButton — flat, chrome-less image buttons that reproduce the WinForms
        FlatStyle.Flat + FlatAppearance.BorderSize=0 + BackColor=Transparent buttons: just the glyph,
        with no button surface in any visual state. The :pointerover / :pressed template overrides
        suppress the Fluent hover / press fill that would otherwise box the transparent glyph (the
        same technique used by the sibling FormHelpView / FormPanView / Keypad controls).

        Button.numBox — nudSnapDistance is rendered as a Button styled like a STATIC numeric field
        (the WinForms NudlessNumericUpDown was a read-only numeric box whose click opened a keypad):
        an AliceBlue face with a 1px grey border that stays put across hover / press, so it reads as
        a value box rather than a glowing button.
    -->
    <Window.Styles>
        <Style Selector="Button.imageButton">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.imageButton:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.imageButton:pressed /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
        </Style>

        <Style Selector="Button.numBox">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="AliceBlue" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Gray" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1" />
            <!-- Square corners: the WinForms NudlessNumericUpDown is a square-edged numeric field;
                 pin CornerRadius=0 so the Fluent theme's default rounded corners do not soften it. -->
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="Black" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.numBox /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="AliceBlue" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.numBox:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="AliceBlue" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Gray" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.numBox:pressed /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="AliceBlue" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Gray" />
        </Style>
    </Window.Styles>

    <!--
        Root Canvas reproduces the WinForms absolute layout 1:1: every Canvas.Left / Canvas.Top +
        Width / Height equals the exact designer Location / Size on the 223 x 396 client. Combined
        with the window's SizeToContent this yields a client area of exactly 223 x 396.
    -->
    <Canvas Width="223" Height="396">

        <!--
            WhiteSmoke panel — stands in for the WinForms `tableLayoutPanel1`
            (FormRefNudge.designer.cs lines 84-105): BackColor WhiteSmoke, Location (21,14),
            Size 182 x 263. The original TableLayoutPanel arranged its five children in a 2-column
            grid; here their exact designer Location / Size are reproduced on an inner Canvas for
            pixel-accurate parity.
        -->
        <Border Canvas.Left="21" Canvas.Top="14"
                Width="182" Height="263"
                Background="WhiteSmoke">
            <Canvas Width="182" Height="263">

                <!-- btnHalfToolLeft — nudge half-tool-width LEFT. Designer (10,21) 69x58, glyph SnapLeftHalf. -->
                <Button x:Name="btnHalfToolLeft"
                        Classes="imageButton"
                        Canvas.Left="10" Canvas.Top="21"
                        Width="69" Height="58"
                        HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                        VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Nudge half tool width left">
                    <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/SnapLeftHalf.png" Stretch="Uniform" />
                </Button>

                <!-- btnHalfToolRight — nudge half-tool-width RIGHT. Designer (101,21) 69x58, glyph
                     SnapRightHalf. (The WinForms designer set ImageAlign=MiddleRight on this single
                     button; like the other three arrows it is rendered with a centred uniform glyph
                     here — visually equivalent at this scale and consistent with the file spec's
                     uniform treatment of all four arrow buttons.) -->
                <Button x:Name="btnHalfToolRight"
                        Classes="imageButton"
                        Canvas.Left="101" Canvas.Top="21"
                        Width="69" Height="58"
                        HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                        VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Nudge half tool width right">
                    <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/SnapRightHalf.png" Stretch="Uniform" />
                </Button>

                <!-- btnAdjLeft — nudge by snap distance LEFT. Designer (10,122) 69x58, glyph SnapLeft. -->
                <Button x:Name="btnAdjLeft"
                        Classes="imageButton"
                        Canvas.Left="10" Canvas.Top="122"
                        Width="69" Height="58"
                        HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                        VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Nudge left by snap distance">
                    <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/SnapLeft.png" Stretch="Uniform" />
                </Button>

                <!-- btnAdjRight — nudge by snap distance RIGHT. Designer (101,122) 69x58, glyph SnapRight. -->
                <Button x:Name="btnAdjRight"
                        Classes="imageButton"
                        Canvas.Left="101" Canvas.Top="122"
                        Width="69" Height="58"
                        HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                        VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Nudge right by snap distance">
                    <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/SnapRight.png" Stretch="Uniform" />
                </Button>

                <!-- nudSnapDistance — read-only snap-distance display (WinForms NudlessNumericUpDown,
                     ReadOnly, Maximum 1000, Value 800, Tahoma 18pt Bold centred). Designer (37,214)
                     107x36. Rendered as a numeric-box Button (Classes="numBox"); the "8" is a
                     design-time placeholder the code-behind overwrites, and a click opens the
                     numeric keypad. -->
                <Button x:Name="nudSnapDistance"
                        Classes="numBox"
                        Canvas.Left="37" Canvas.Top="214"
                        Width="107" Height="36"
                        FontSize="24" FontWeight="Bold"
                        HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                        VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                        Content="8" />

            </Canvas>
        </Border>

        <!-- lblOffset — running total offset readout. WinForms Label (16,289) 187x31, Tahoma 18pt
             Bold (-> 24 DIP), ForeColor Black, transparent, TextAlign MiddleCenter, Text "0.0 cm"
             (placeholder; code-behind sets it to e.g. "12 cm"). A 24 DIP line fills the 31px band,
             so the single line reads as vertically centred. -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="lblOffset"
                   Canvas.Left="16" Canvas.Top="289"
                   Width="187" Height="31"
                   FontSize="24" FontWeight="Bold"
                   Foreground="Black"
                   Background="Transparent"
                   TextAlignment="Center"
                   Text="0.0 cm" />

        <!-- btnCancelMain — roll the track list back and close. WinForms Button (3,334) 78x57,
             FlatStyle.Flat, BorderSize 0, BackColor Transparent, glyph Cancel64. -->
        <Button x:Name="btnCancelMain"
                Classes="imageButton"
                Canvas.Left="3" Canvas.Top="334"
                Width="78" Height="57"
                HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                AutomationProperties.Name="Cancel">
            <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/Cancel64.png" Stretch="Uniform" />
        </Button>

        <!-- btnExit — commit (save tracks) and close. WinForms Button (111,334) 106x57,
             FlatStyle.Flat, BorderSize 0, BackColor Transparent, glyph OK64 with
             ImageAlign=MiddleRight (-> the glyph is right-aligned via HorizontalContentAlignment=
             "Right" plus an explicit 56x56 image so it fits the 57px-tall button). The WinForms
             Tahoma 15.75pt Bold (-> 21 DIP) + ForeColor ARGB(192,64,0) = #FFC04000 are preserved as
             COSMETIC only — the source assigns NO Text, so the button shows the glyph alone. -->
        <Button x:Name="btnExit"
                Classes="imageButton"
                Canvas.Left="111" Canvas.Top="334"
                Width="106" Height="57"
                FontSize="21" FontWeight="Bold"
                Foreground="#FFC04000"
                HorizontalContentAlignment="Right"
                VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                AutomationProperties.Name="OK">
            <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/OK64.png"
                   Width="56" Height="56" Stretch="Uniform" />
        </Button>

    </Canvas>
</Window>
